  "rules": "Quick-Draw Duels:\n\nIn this land, justice is often decided in a heartbeat — or the failure of one.\n\n- When a duel begins, both participants roll a closed Oracle question:\n“Do I outdraw my opponent?”\nUse Advantage if tags support it (e.g. Quick Hands, Fast Reflexes, Gunfighter Instinct).\n- The winner gains Advantage on their first Conflict roll.\n\nAfter that, combat proceeds normally — each side takes turns resolving Conflicts until one is down, disarmed, or flees.\n\nWanted Levels:\n\nA good name goes a long way in the West. A bad one goes even further.\n\nEach time you commit crimes or notorious acts, your **Wanted Level** increases. Higher levels draw the attention of lawmen, bounty hunters, and the occasional vigilante. Good deeds may reduce your notoriety — but only if someone’s watching.\n\n**Wanted Levels:**\n\n1. **Unknown** – You're a nobody. Free to roam.\n2. **Petty Criminal** – You've stolen, lied, or trespassed. Some folks might take note.\n3. **Notorious Outlaw** – There's a poster with your face on it somewhere.\n4. **Infamous Gang Leader** – You're a known threat. Most towns will refuse you service or shoot on sight.\n5. **Public Enemy** – Your name spreads faster than your horse can ride. You’re hunted.\n6. **Legendary Outlaw** – You’re a living myth. The law wants your head. So does half the territory.\n\n> **Tip:** Some towns or factions may react based on your level. At Level 3+, roll Faction Tags with Disadvantage unless disguised or protected.\n\nHardship:\n\nThe frontier doesn’t care about your plans. It breaks them — and you — without apology.\n\n- You must track **thirst**, **hunger**, and **exposure**.\n- When injured, healing is slow unless you have access to clean water, shelter, or proper medicine.\n- Harsh conditions (drought, dust storms, blizzards) may impose penalties or force checks to continue travel or avoid Frailty Tags.\n\n> **Example:**\n> You’re stranded on the mesa. No water, no shade. After a day’s travel, you gain the tag `Parched`. Keep it until you find water. If `Parched` is still active and you fail a survival check, gain `Delirious` or `Sunburned`.\n\n> **Note:** Use Frailty Tags like `Starving`, `Frostbitten`, or `Exhausted` to represent long-term hardship effects.",
  "locations": [
    {
      "label": "Red Lantern Saloon",
      "detail": "Faded hub of drink, smoke, and whispered deals. Known for poker games that end in gunfire.",
      "encounters": "Bartender, Drifter, Card Shark"
    },
    {
      "label": "Devil’s Spine Pass",
      "detail": "Narrow switchback trail carved through jagged rock. Ideal ground for ambushes — or accidents.",
      "encounters": "Highwayman, Scout, Coyote"
    },
    {
      "label": "Lost Pick Mine",
      "detail": "Partially collapsed claim with rumors of hidden silver. Echoes travel too far down here.",
      "encounters": "Claim Jumper, Stray Mule, Cave-In Risk"
    },
    {
      "label": "Fort Redemption",
      "detail": "Old Union fort turned garrison for local patrols. Supplies are short, tempers shorter.",
      "encounters": "Captain, Deserter, Supply Officer"
    },
    {
      "label": "Dusthaven",
      "detail": "Boomtown gone bust, now ruled by backroom politics. Streets are dry, but blood still runs.",
      "encounters": "Corrupt Mayor, Deputy, Loan Shark"
    },
    {
      "label": "Hollow Tree Ranch",
      "detail": "Well-fenced spread on disputed land. Guards work for pay — and switch sides fast.",
      "encounters": "Ranch Hand, Foreman, Trespasser"
    }
  ],
  "seeds": [
    "Track counterfeit coin to a printing press hidden in a traveling medicine show.",
    "Track a bounty into storm country, but the outlaw’s kin are watching every ridge.",
    "You wake with your gear stolen and a sheriff’s badge pinned to your chest. The town calls you law now.",
    "Dig into a sudden election victory — the votes outnumber the living in town.",
    "Investigate a string of barn burnings blamed on a rival ranch — but something doesn’t add up.",
    "Escort a supply wagon through contested range land as both raiders and ranchers stake their claim.",
    "A cattle baron's son vanished on a trail ride. Find him before the vultures do.",
    "Ride escort for a payroll wagon rumored to be double-loaded. Word’s out, and so are the wolves.",
    "Serve a warrant in a boomtown that hasn't seen a lawman in years. No one wants the man found.",
    "Locate a missing surveyor last seen camping near Devil’s Spine — his camp is burned and his horse shot.",
    "Protect a railworker strike leader from hired enforcers. The company says she’s a firebrand.",
    "Escort a prisoner across county lines — their old gang has set up blockades.",
    "Break into a war profiteer’s warehouse to recover stolen army rifles before they cross the border.",
    "Guard a bridge under construction. Dynamite’s gone missing, and tempers are short.",
    "A former outlaw seeks to surrender. His old partners plan to bury him before he can talk.",
    "Break a siege: a traveling doctor and her patients are trapped in a church by local vigilantes.",
    "Trail a stolen herd across open range. Something’s killing cattle and leaving the meat behind.",
    "Confront a gunman killing veterans from the same company. You wore the same uniform once.",
    "A caravan of settlers seeks escort — but a masked rider follows, asking for one man’s head.",
    "A judge arrives in town with a docket of buried sins. Keep them alive through the night.",
    "Defend a widow's homestead from hired guns sent by a railroad syndicate with forged land claims.",
    "You’re offered coin to testify in a land dispute. Both sides swear they’ll kill you if you do.",
    "Transport a coffin to a mountain cemetery. The family says to bury it before nightfall.",
    "Investigate a mine collapse blamed on sabotage. Survivors say it wasn’t just the rocks that moved.",
    "Follow a boot trail into the canyons. The man you’re after vanished chasing a mirage.",
    "Negotiate a truce between two ranches after a shootout left three men dead — and the water rights in question.",
    "Intercept a telegram before it reaches the governor. Some truths don’t travel safe in daylight.",
    "Stop a jailbreak planned by the sheriff’s own deputy. The town’s split, and time’s running short.",
    "A land baron pays handsomely to relocate a family. The family refuses to move — or to speak.",
    "A letter arrives: your name is on a will, but the town holding the inheritance is run by outlaws.",
    "A homesteader’s well turns to blood. Panic brews, but someone stands to gain from the exodus.",
    "Protect a mule train carrying dynamite to the mountain mine — snow’s coming and wolves follow.",
    "An aging lawman asks for your help arresting his own son. The town’s ready to turn against him.",
    "A storm uncovers graves on land newly claimed. The sheriff wants it quiet. The preacher does not.",
    "A band of regulators offers justice. Are they law — or just another gang with clean boots?",
    "A hired scout hasn’t returned from the high pass. Their horse came back alone and bloody."
  ],
